 Play a key role in coordinating the budgeting process, including consolidation, critical analysis of assumptions and providing management with meaningful insight into financial results;
 Develop, enhance and interpret strategic key performance indicators (KPIs) to support management decisions and the optimal allocation of capital;
 Design and maintain executive dashboards and decision-support tools, with a focus on clarity, relevance and added value for managers;
 Act as a trusted advisor to investment teams on financial performance, interpretation of results and the financial impacts of operational decisions;
 Ensure the ongoing development and robustness of the costing model for investment activities, promoting consistency, transparency and accuracy in allocated costs;
 Contribute to the governance of financial processes related to the preparation and analysis of monthly, quarterly and annual financial statements, with a strong focus on the quality and reliability of financial information;
 Perform and oversee complex accounting analyses, including journal entries, reconciliations and taxes, while serving as a point of reference on matters requiring a high degree of professional judgment;
 Work closely with internal partners to structure, analyze and clarify the financial treatment of certain expenses and strategic initiatives;
 Identify and implement continuous improvements to financial management processes to enhance efficiency, rigor and decision-making.
 What could accelerate your success in this role
